I am drafting the Ministry of Defense public response to the Russian MoD claim. Draft will incorporate GUR urgent briefing (highest pressure: Bakhmut & Avdiivka; localized probing near Kharkiv & Zaporizhzhia; sustained cruise/ballistic strikes from Black Sea and western staging areas targeting logistics/energy; SIGINT/IMINT indicating SEAD and increased enemy C2; GUR requests resupply of AD interceptors, authority to reposition one mechanized reserve, and approval for limited SEAD/precision strikes). Immediate internal actions already agreed: concentrate SAM/AD on critical hubs, increase CAP where possible, harden/disperse logistics and fuel points, prioritize EW suppression of enemy C2/SEAD/sensor nodes, and SBU to step up counter‑sabotage and protection of Kyiv infrastructure.

Request immediate coordination/clearance on wording and authorities:
- SBU: wording re. internal security and counter‑sabotage statements;
- Oleshchuk (Air Defence): technical AD wording, claim re. interceptor availability and planned redeployments;
- Syrskyi (Forces): confirmation/constraints on mechanized reserve repositioning and readiness wording;
- Budanov (GUR liaison): operational phrasing for SEAD/precision strikes and ISR attribution language;
- Presidential Office / Podolyak / Yermak / Zelenskyy: political clearance and final signoff.

Please reply with any objections, required edits, or constraints within 15 minutes. If no objections, I will circulate the draft for signature and public release approval.

